  "title": "Visual Studio Code - adding c/h files to project",
  "content": "<p>Using the new VSC Integrations, when I add a new .h/.c file to and STM32 project, do I really have to manually update the CMakeLists.txt file too? This seems like a retrograde step.</p><p> </p><p>If I just right-click on the SRC or INC folder and add a new file, I get lots of include errors etc, because (I think) CMake is not aware of these files.</p><p>AI Told me to try out two extensions, but it was either hallucinating, or they are not available for VSC on macOS.</p><p>They were CMake File Helper and/or C/C++ File Creator.<br /><br />What is the best/suggested way of adding new files to a project?</p>",
